WEBVTT

00:01:57.655 --> 00:02:00.992
run on more than 98% clean energy.

00:02:01.826 --> 00:02:05.288
But most dispatch curves contain
more of a mix

00:02:05.288 --> 00:02:08.791
of carbon-free and carbon-emitting
energy sources.

00:02:09.125 --> 00:02:12.170
This means that where your electricity
is coming from—

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:15.631
and how clean it is— 
varies throughout the day—

00:02:15.631 --> 00:02:18.050
as often as every few minutes.

00:02:18.634 --> 00:02:20.636
Take the state of Kansas.

00:02:20.636 --> 00:02:23.097
Despite having plentiful wind resources,

00:02:23.097 --> 00:02:26.976
it regularly relies on carbon-emitting 
power plants.

00:02:26.976 --> 00:02:30.354
This is because wind energy is especially
plentiful at night.